> ## Task Budgets (Quick Reference) (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>
> **Beta, Claude Opus 5 / Claude Opus 5.5 / Fable 5 / Claude Fable 5.1 (confirm at launch) / Claude Sonnet 5.5 / Claude Haiku 5.5 / Opus 4.8 / 4.7 (not Claude Sonnet 5).** A task budget gives Claude a token ceiling for an agentic loop so it paces itself and finishes gracefully instead of being cut off - distinct from `max_tokens`, which is an enforced per-response ceiling the model is not aware of. Minimum `total`: 20,000. Set `task_budget` inside `output_config` on `client.beta.messages.stream(...)` with beta flag `task-budgets-2026-03-13` - use streaming so the large `max_tokens` doesn't hit HTTP timeouts (full details: `shared/model-migration.md` -> Task Budgets): (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>
> ```python (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
> with client.beta.messages.stream( (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>     model="claude-opus-5-5", max_tokens=128000, (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>     output_config={"effort": "high", "task_budget": {"type": "tokens", "total": 64000}}, (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>     betas=["task-budgets-2026-03-13"], (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>     messages=[...], tools=[...], (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
> ) as stream: (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>     response = stream.get_final_message() (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
> ``` (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>
> `task_budget` fields: `type` (always `"tokens"`), `total`, and optional `remaining` (defaults to `total`). The server injects a countdown marker Claude sees during generation; the budget counts what Claude generates and the tool results it reads this turn - **not** the full history you resend each request. Not the same thing as **Managed Agents session budgets** - those are hard, dollar-denominated, platform-enforced caps on one CMA session (`shared/managed-agents-core.md` § Session budgets); a task budget is advisory and token-denominated. (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>
> **Observing spend:** accumulate `response.usage.output_tokens` (plus the token count of the tool-result blocks you append) across loop iterations if you want to display progress. Leave `remaining` unset in the normal loop - the server tracks the countdown itself, and passing a client-computed `remaining` while also resending full history under-reports the budget. **Only pass `remaining`** when you compact or rewrite history between requests and the server can no longer derive prior spend. (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
