> ## Common Pitfalls (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
>
> - Don't truncate inputs when passing files or content to the API. If the content is too long to fit in the context window, notify the user and discuss options (chunking, summarization, etc.) rather than silently truncating. (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
> - **Prefill removed (Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, and the 4.6/4.7/4.8 family):** Assistant message prefills (last-assistant-turn prefills) return a 400 error on Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Haiku 5.5, Opus 4.6, Opus 4.7, Opus 4.8, and Sonnet 4.6. Use structured outputs (`output_config.format`) or system prompt instructions to control response format instead. (One exception: the fallback-credit prefill claim - when redeeming a credit with `fallback_has_prefill_claim: true`, the server accepts the echoed assistant message; see the migration guide's refusal section.) (23 October 2026, 17:18:17 +0200)
